% \begin{macro}{\hep_math_accent:nnn}
% \begin{macro}{\__hep_math_accent_shape:}
% The accent font \file{hepaccent.ttf} contains the accents derived from the serif, sans-serif and bold \NCM math fonts as consecutive private use characters, starting at the character "#3".
% Like the script families it is allocated past the limit of the \LaTeX\ kernel at the beginning of the document.
% \software{luaotfload} only reads the accent attachments of its math table with the math script, which is passed directly, because \software{fontspec} only recognises scripts with features.
% Each accent selects the shape matching the math font of the math version, whose vector accent is used by "\vec", and is fixed in size like "\vec".
