# The `hep-math-font` package

Composable math alphabets that follow the text font, and dashed and
dotted vector accents

## Introduction

The `hep-math-font` package provides math fonts matching the text fonts
of the `hep-font` package. Its math alphabet commands are composable:
bold, upright and the serif, sans-serif and typewriter families can be
combined in any order, e.g. `\mathbf{\mathsf{x}}` and
`\mathsf{\mathbf{x}}` give the same bold sans-serif x. Math follows the
surrounding text, so that math in a sans-serif or bold heading is
sans-serif or bold as well. The package also provides vector accents
with a dashed and a dotted shaft. With LuaLaTeX and XeLaTeX the package
uses the New Computer Modern math fonts, with pdfLaTeX it uses Latin
Modern and Computer Modern fonts combined into virtual fonts.

The package is loaded using `\usepackage{hep-math-font}`.

